<header><p class="st-kicker">khanate · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Khanate of Maragheh</h1><p class="st-meta">1747 CE – 1800 CE (approx.) · capital Maragheh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A local khanate of the Muqaddam tribe around Maragheh, the old Ilkhanid capital, in the decades between the Afsharids and the Qajars.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah's</a> death in 1747, the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maragha">Maragheh</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>, and its fertile district came under the hereditary control of khans of the Muqaddam tribe. Maragheh had been the first capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and site of Nasir al-Din al-Tusi's observatory.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Muqaddam khans ruled a small agricultural region of orchards and vineyards near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-urmia">Lake Urmia</a>, maintaining their own troops and paying tribute to the dominant power of the moment, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/zand-empire">Zand Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-khan-muqaddam">Ahmad Khan Muqaddam</a> is the best-known ruler. They were in frequent conflict with the khans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urmia">Urmia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agha-mohammad-khan-qajar">Agha Mohammad Khan</a>'s <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/qajar-iran">Qajar Iran</a> subdued the Azerbaijani khanates in the 1790s, and around 1800 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maragha">Maragheh</a> was absorbed, its Muqaddam khans continuing as governors under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajars</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="khanate, 1747 CE – 1800 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">khanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.47%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1747 CE – 1800 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>khanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Maragheh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ahmad Khan Muqaddam</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Azerbaijani Turkic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Maragheh Khanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=khanate-of-maragheh" aria-label="Khanate of Maragheh on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5836 832 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khanate of Maragheh lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6156 1088L6298 1144M6156 1088L6364 1269"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6298 1144h0M6364 1269h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6156 1088h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6156 1088h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Maragheh. <a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=khanate-of-maragheh">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

